<!DOCTYPE RCC><RCC version="1.0">
    <!-- Runtime paths are :/fonts/NAME - flat, as cards.qrc and table.qrc are,
         so the per-family folders on disk are not part of any URL.

         NEVER WRITE THE ENTRY TAG'S NAME IN ANGLE BRACKETS IN A COMMENT HERE. The
         dependency scan qt_add_resources() generates is a regex over this file,
         not an XML parser: it reads a bracketed tag name inside a comment as the
         start of an entry, swallows everything up to the next real closing tag
         as a "path", and writes that into the Makefile, which then fails with
         "missing separator". That is how this comment's first draft broke the
         build.

         The redesign's three typefaces (docs/ui-redesign/ section 2.3), all from
         Google Fonts under the SIL Open Font License. fonts::registerBundled()
         loads every .ttf here; it is the only reader.

         THE LICENCES ARE EMBEDDED TOO. The OFL lets a font ship inside a program
         on condition that its copyright notice and licence go with it, and this
         binary is the only thing that ships - so the three licence texts travel
         in it beside the fonts they cover. Each family has its own copyright line,
         which is why there are three and not one. -->
    <qresource prefix="/fonts">
        <file alias="CinzelDecorative-Bold.ttf">fonts/cinzel-decorative/CinzelDecorative-Bold.ttf</file>
        <file alias="Belleza-Regular.ttf">fonts/belleza/Belleza-Regular.ttf</file>
        <file alias="AlegreyaSans-Regular.ttf">fonts/alegreya-sans/AlegreyaSans-Regular.ttf</file>
        <file alias="AlegreyaSans-Medium.ttf">fonts/alegreya-sans/AlegreyaSans-Medium.ttf</file>
        <file alias="AlegreyaSans-Bold.ttf">fonts/alegreya-sans/AlegreyaSans-Bold.ttf</file>

        <file alias="OFL-CinzelDecorative.txt">fonts/cinzel-decorative/OFL.txt</file>
        <file alias="OFL-Belleza.txt">fonts/belleza/OFL.txt</file>
        <file alias="OFL-AlegreyaSans.txt">fonts/alegreya-sans/OFL.txt</file>
    </qresource>
</RCC>
